OL,3,GNEWSACities bid to host Women's World
OL,4,ACup matches
OL,5,
OL,6,FFormer Newcastle United and England
OL,7,Fstar Jordan Nobbs said the tournament
OL,8,Fwould help the women's game "grow even
OL,9,Fmore", while Sunderland chief operating
OL,10,FOfficer, Tim Greenwell said hosting
OL,11,F"would help the club and the city".
OL,13,FThe UK was the only country to bid for
OL,14,Fthe tournament that will see 104
OL,15,Fmatches contested by 48 teams over 39
OL,16,Fdays.
